# CITATION.cff — released. Author list, order and ORCID confirmed; Zenodo concept DOI
# minted (10.5281/zenodo.21769959) and recorded below. The "DRAFT" header that used to sit
# here outlived every condition it named.
#
# Second author added 2026-09-22, for v0.2.0: Pierluigi Cerulo, same person and same ORCID as
# `paper/paper.md`'s co-author, added there for project direction. Zenodo takes its creators
# list from this file, not from paper.md, so the two are kept in the same order deliberately —
# see the `authors:` block's own comment below for why.
#
# Licence: AGPL-3.0-or-later, consistent across LICENSE, pyproject.toml and this
# file — verified 2026-08-02. (The earlier note here claiming LICENSE held GPL-3.0
# text was stale; it holds the AGPL, 661 lines with the network-server preamble.)
# GitHub's licensee still *displays* GPL-3.0, which is a detection artefact and
# is tracked as an issue, not a licensing inconsistency.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EROTICA, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "EROTICA: Estimation, Recovery & Optimization, together with Inference, for Cluster Analysis"
# "calibrated" dropped from the abstract below 2026-09-22 to match paper/paper.md: the
# package ships calibration diagnostics (reliability checks), it does not assert its own
# output is calibrated -- that is an empirical claim the companion methods paper has to
# make, not this metadata file.
abstract: >-
  An integrated Bayesian Python pipeline for identifying and characterizing
  open clusters in Gaia data: HDBSCAN pseudo-probability membership with
  Bayesian PM/parallax refinement, Bayesian King structural fitting, NUTS
  Poisson-Hess isochrone fitting, membership-calibration diagnostics, and
  dynamical diagnostics, with ArviZ InferenceData provenance for every fit.
type: software
authors:
  # This list is also the Zenodo deposit's author list: the archive IS the software, so they are
  # decided together with paper/paper.md's author list, not independently.
  - family-names: "Pulgar-Escobar"
    given-names: "Lucas"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Concepción, Chile"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4359-2444"
  # Added 2026-09-22, for v0.2.0: same ORCID and affiliation as paper/paper.md's co-author,
  # added there for project direction. Order matches the paper.
  - family-names: "Cerulo"
    given-names: "Pierluigi"
    affiliation: "Departamento de Ingeniería Informática y Ciencias de la Computación, Universidad de Concepción, Chile"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0703-3123"
repository-code: "https://github.com/notluquis/erotica"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21769959   # concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version

# Once the NGC 6383 A&A paper has a DOI, uncomment this block. GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" button then points at the paper instead of the software entry, which
# is the correct target for a methods paper with a companion code release.
#
# preferred-citation:
#   type: article
#   title: "<paper title>"
#   authors:
#     - family-names: Pulgar
#       given-names: "Lucas M."
#   journal: "Astronomy & Astrophysics"
#   year: 2026
#   doi: "<10.1051/0004-6361/...>"
